# fixedbugs, defect 157, lane land186, 2026-10-02 (panel 186 R9), the
# coordinator's `tu1.hero`.
#
# SYMPTOM: `record UI tag utag` over a header's `union utag` was refused with
# a note saying *a group's `record` is the header's STRUCT. A union has no
# `record` spelling in this language*, while `record W` over a typedef'd union
# builds and reads; and no golden held the code.
#
# FIX: the refusal stays (panel 186's R9 question); its note says what is true:
# a `record` binds a union by a typedef's name, the header's or one of the
# program's own, and otherwise a `ptr` reaches it.

extern "fixedbugs-157-unions.h"
    record UI tag utag  #~ ffi_tag_is_a_union
        i: i32
    function make_u() -> UI

function main()
    print(make_u().i)
